Z||000000||mutfish||10-31-1999||10:09 PM||||I,m just about ready to reassemble my gt after repaint and need all the goofy rivets and such,anyone know of a good source or how about a good subsitute for any of them....||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cooter||10-31-1999||11:12 PM||||I went to Ace hardware and got some 1/4 inch drywall fasteners. They look like white plastic rivets with a metal pin in the middle. The fit on some of these was a little loose, so I backed them up with a small flat washer to take up some of the slack. They worked great, are removeable, reuseable and very inexpensive. ||||reg||14
Z||000002||Dan||11-01-1999||06:36 AM|||| Try the dealership or body shop or supplier.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||11-01-1999||07:56 AM||||I know Ed Parks has them at the Fiero Factory.  I saw them on the shelf when I picked up my new motor.<BR>Write to him at<P>Fierofactory@juno.com<BR>or call (256) 420-5391||||reg||1
Z||000004||peterh||11-01-1999||08:50 AM||||I got the plastic pop rivets from the Fiero store to put my rocker panel back on. I got a special plastic pop rivet tool from my local autobody supply store for $25.00. They also have plastic rivets. Unfortunately the plastic rivets did not compress properly and I ended up using some regular aluminum pop rivets. The reason for using plastic rivets is they have some give to them so the plastic will not crack. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||dogtired||11-01-1999||01:44 PM||||Yesterday I noticed on my 92 Grand Am the shroud on top of the radiator is held on by the same type of fastener so I would try a dealer?||||reg||3
Z||000006||theogre||11-01-1999||03:15 PM||||There are plastic screw rivits at pep boys.... I don't have the part # handy. It's a Rivit tite product usually on the rack with bolts and things. they are about a $1.50us for a pair. they look stock and you can take them apart again if need be. You want the 1/4 inch diam ones. If you need allot get them from a dealler or try Napa level shops that have bigger selections.||||reg||1
